arm_smmu + qcom_iommu_util (soc-repo forks): 6.18 IOMMU core

The forks stay: the vendor DT's SMMUs are "qcom,qsmmu-v500" (upstream arm-smmu does not match
it), and kgsl, msm_drm, camera, coresight-tmc and ipam call qcom_iommu_util APIs that only
work through the qcom_iommu_ops the forked arm_smmu registers (see PORT-STATUS.md).

- arm-smmu: iommu_fwspec_free() is gone (the core frees the fwspec on a failed probe).
- arm-smmu: iommu_ops.pgsize_bitmap is gone; every paging domain carries its own from
  allocation (as upstream 6.18: smmu->pgsize_bitmap, narrowed to the io-pgtable's on attach
  as before), and the global "restricted during device attach" accumulation goes.
- arm-smmu: iommu_domain_ops.enable_nesting is gone (iommufd nest parents replaced it); the
  vendor stack has no caller.
- io-pgtable-fast, qcom-io-pgtable-alloc: the struct-page helpers __iommu_alloc_pages() /
  __iommu_free_pages() of the 6.12 drivers/iommu/iommu-pages.h are gone; local versions over
  iommu_alloc_pages_node_sz()/iommu_free_pages() (same NR_IOMMU_PAGES /
  NR_SECONDARY_PAGETABLE accounting). Every caller allocates and frees single pages.

